Level 0 — Initial SSH Connection

WHAT THIS LEVEL IS ABOUT : 

=> This is the entry point to the Bandit wargame. The objective is to establish an SSH connection to the game server. SSH (Secure Shell) is a cryptographic protocol for securely accessing remote machines — a foundational skill for any Linux or security professional.


APPROACH : 

The first step I took was to resolve the server's IP address using nslookup before connecting:
nslookup bandit.labs.overthewire.org

This confirmed the server was reachable. I then connected via SSH on the non-standard port 2220:
ssh bandit0@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Entered bandit0 as the password when prompted. Connection established successfully.

KEY TAKEAWAY : 
The -p 2220 flag overrides SSH's default port 22. Every level in Bandit uses this port.
